win-full: Windows R 4.6.2, variant full.

Not generated: Windows has no configure. config.h and Rconfig.h are R's
own src/gnuwin32/fixed/h/ files (GENERATED_FROM names the R version),
with r-zig's edits:
- HAVE_CURL_CURL_H and HAVE_LIBCURL defined (the internet module).
- USE_ICU, HAVE_OPENMP and SUPPORT_OPENMP defined where the variant has
  ICU and OpenMP.
- The defines that build.zig's variant table names (Features,
  checkVariantConfig) flipped to the variant's value: ENABLE_NLS
  (config.h and Rconfig.h), HAVE_TCLTK, HAVE_JPEG, HAVE_TIFF,
  HAVE_TIFFIO_H, HAVE_PNG, USE_ICU, HAVE_LIBDEFLATE, HAVE_LIBDEFLATE_H,
  USE_LIBDEFLATE, HAVE_OPENMP, HAVE_OPENMP_SIMDRED, SUPPORT_OPENMP.
subst.txt is written by hand: the link lists of upstream's Makefile.win
files, one key per feature (BITMAP_LIBS, TCLTK_LIBS, CAIRO_LIBS,
BUILD_DEVCAIRO_TRUE, R_OPENMP_CFLAGS, SHLIB_OPENMP_CFLAGS, and the
Windows-only ICU_LIBS and LIBDEFLATE_LIBS), plus the WIN_* lists every
variant shares. etc/x64/Makeconf comes from ../win-common/Makeconf.win.
build.zig checks every file here against the variant table on each
build, and stops on a mismatch.
